      "lineNbr": 196,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T14:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this because we are calling `recordForwards` for stencil draws when it\u0027s a step \u003e 0, so we want to start on the layer after the first stencil draw step?\n\nRegardless, I think this is subtle enough that we should explain what `bound` is doing here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 196,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "cd3c9e443a01e0c9d9af091961598c15cdcd207b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a04c691_d75bfb67",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawListLayer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 196,
      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-09T14:01:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is this because we are calling recordForwards for stencil draws when it\u0027s a step \u003e 0\n\nYes\n\n\u003e so we want to start on the layer after the first stencil draw step\n\nNo! By ratcheting the starting list forward, we *avoid* intersection with our parent stencil draw, so we *do not* create a new layer. If we did not do this, stencils would be guaranteed to make a new layer for each step in the renderer.",
      "parentUuid": "361391a4_6a40f977",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 196,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "cd3c9e443a01e0c9d9af091961598c15cdcd207b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "681c3d89_3f228621",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawListLayer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T14:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All the current stencil-based renderers have all steps that useing stencil buffer (either for reading or writing), even if they are the shading step. I think we can just say that it\u0027s convenient to treat the entire renderer as using the stencil buffer, but we could move the rendererIsStencil check into the for loop and look it up from just the step\u0027s flags.\n\nOn the other hand, the pilot draw system is also enforcing the the logical ordering of render steps executing in the order they were declared by the renderer, even if the renderer didn\u0027t use stencil buffers. We don\u0027t have any renderer that uses multiple steps that doesn\u0027t use stencil buffers, but this behavior is probably worth calling out as part of recordForwards.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 89,
        "endLine": 249,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "cd3c9e443a01e0c9d9af091961598c15cdcd207b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
